# Error Handling

Classify errors as: caller input, configuration, temporary/permanent provider, tool execution, database, authentication, or internal application errors.

For every failure:

- Log with correlation identifiers
- Avoid exposing implementation details to the caller
- Use safe retry behavior; do not retry non-idempotent actions blindly
- Provide a natural caller-facing response
- Escalate or end the call safely when recovery is not possible

Do not continue a conversation as though an action succeeded when it failed.
